   2012  fcf7							; --- D6 M1 (left-col block): M1X = 8*(m1_col+1)-1 -> CollisionEndX ($8E) ---
   2013  fcf7							; 0 = no M1 patch. Window: this VBL write -> PositionBallM1 reads it
   2014  fcf7							; later the same VBL (staged-file pattern like Temp/BallX). Overscan
   2015  fcf7							; routines (PHM/LWC/blast/laser) restage their own CollisionEndX values
   2016  fcf7							; AFTER the cave read, so the alias never crosses a frame boundary.
   2017  fcf7							; NOT zeroed with BandTab on strip kill — M1 is a whole-cave latch and
   2018  fcf7							; convert guarantees its cell is solid/unpatched (wall) where it must hide.
   2019  fcf7							; M1 strip DESTROYED (EnemyDeadMask b4, StripBlastCheck's M1 twin) →
   2020  fcf7							; stage 0: PositionBallM1 skips ENAM1, the pack's b3 flag clears, and
   2021  fcf7							; both overlay paths (PHM/blast) treat the strip as gone next frame.
   2022  fcf7		       a5 99		      lda	RoomMetaA
