   2092  fd39							; Door stripe color ($8D) is staged inside PhaseBlink (this window
   2093  fd39							; was full to the $F4C4 pin, retired 2026-10-20 — the 14B staging
   2094  fd39							; block lives with the walk where there is hole).
   2095  fd39							; --- Phase 3: phase-cell blink (PF buffer pokes) ----------------------
   2096  fd39							; Body moved after the level data (PhaseBlink, ~130B — the StageBandTab
   2097  fd39							; window $F3C4..$F4C4 was full; the data window has the only free
   2098  fd39							; hole). Contract: clobbers A/X/Y/FetchPtr/RectCount/LineCount/
   2099  fd39							; CollisionCellX/CollisionEndY ($8F scratch — the pack below rebuilds
   2100  fd39							; it). The PF buffers ARE the collision map (cell walk + laser read
   2101  fd39							; them) — toggling the cell's two bits THERE makes render + PHM +
   2102  fd39							; laser follow with zero kernel cost. 64f full cycle = EnemyRamP bit5
   2103  fd39							; (32 on + 32 off; clock-derived, no state bytes — locked plan).
   2104  fd39							; --- PhaseBlink ping-pong (chunk A2): it MUST run after the band/ball
   2105  fd39							; staging above and before the pack below (the crunch walk overwrites
   2106  fd39							; Temp/BandTab for its cell — running it earlier let SBT's own staging
   2107  fd39							; erase the crunch mask, and every crunch kill stopped latching).
   2108  fd39							; Leg 1: this `sta` runs here, the fetch at $F803 is bank2's
   2109  fd39							; `jmp PhBlinkTail` (byte-image pinned in bank2.asm).
   2110  fd39							; --- A3: PhaseBlink is LOCAL now (the record stream lives in bank3) ---
   2111  fd39		       20 d9 f9 	      jsr	PhaseBlink
